# First-party wheels to install into the mdt image.
# One package name per line. Text after '#' is a comment.
# Resolved pre-build by scripts/resolve-devcontainers-release.py; wheels are
# downloaded into pip/wheels/ and installed via `pip install --no-index --find-links`.
#
# Format mirrors apt/packages.list: one entry per line, '#' starts a comment.
#
# Depends on <name>-latest GitHub Release existing at build time.
# The resolver only warns when a release is not found, but the image build then FAILS
# (scripts/check_wheel_set.py): an empty pip/wheels/, or one lacking a name declared
# here, is an error in every build mode.
#
# See: docs/plan-cmru-finish.md §2B (deferred build / cmru-latest dependency).

cli-extended  # https://github.com/volkb79-2/vbpub/releases — cli-extended-v* releases carry the wheel (stdlib-only). cmru declares `cli-extended>=0.3.0` as a real dependency, and the install below is `pip --no-index`, so the cmru wheel can only resolve it from this directory (W3-ZERO Z3). Resolved generically by resolve-devcontainers-release.py via GitHubReleases.resolve_latest; no ordering requirement inside this file.
ciu   # https://github.com/volkb79-2/vbpub/releases — ciu-v* releases carry the wheel (deps Jinja2/PyYAML/tomli_w provided by requirements/toolkit.txt)
cmru  # https://github.com/volkb79-2/vbpub/releases — cmru-v* releases carry the wheel (no runtime deps)
topos  # https://github.com/volkb79-2/vbpub/releases — topos-v* releases carry the wheel (dep textual provided by requirements/toolkit.txt). CLI/client only (`topos --attach`, `topos daemon status|current`) — the root daemon itself needs host DAMON/debugfs/cgroup access this devcontainer does not mount and is not meant to run in a container (see topos/docs/DAEMON.md "Threat Model" + topos/README.md); it connects OUT to a daemon socket, it does not run one in here.
run-gate  # https://github.com/volkb79-2/vbpub/releases — run-gate-v* releases carry the wheel (`run_gate-<ver>-py3-none-any.whl`, stdlib-only, no dependencies). The per-project gate entrypoint (`run-gate <lane>`); gates themselves still run in their declared containers, this only puts the CLI on the cockpit PATH. Not assay (runs from source inside test containers).
cgprofile  # https://github.com/volkb79-2/vbpub/releases — cgprofile-v* releases carry the wheel from 2.0.0 (`cgprofile-<ver>-py3-none-any.whl`, distribution `cgprofile` so it normalizes to the release prefix; the only runtime dependency is cli-extended, already in this file). The cockpit carries the CLIENTS `cgprofile` and `cgprofilectl`; the `cgprofiled` daemon script ships in the same wheel but the daemon runs on the host (installed by host-setup, MDT-055), never in the cockpit. The `report` extra (pandas, plotly, matplotlib, scipy, ruptures) is deliberately NOT in the image closure: `cgprofile report --export-only` works without it and the image installs with `--no-index`.
nyxloom  # https://github.com/volkb79-2/vbpub/releases — nyxloom-v* releases carry the wheel (deps PyYAML/jsonschema/structlog/rich/pygments provided by requirements/toolkit.txt). CLI/dev-tooling only (lint/backlog/registry) — the resident nyxloomd daemon is offline/not deployed; adopting the wheel here does not start or require it.
